===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[take]] [[charge]]|takes charge|taking charge|took charge|taken charge}}

# To [[assume]] [[control]] or [[responsibility]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1898|author={{w|Winston Churchill (novelist)|Winston Churchill}}
|title={{w|The Celebrity}}|chapter=10
|passage=The skipper Mr. Cooke had hired at Far Harbor was a God-fearing man with a luke warm interest in his new billet and employer, and had only been prevailed upon to '''take charge''' of the yacht after the offer of an emolument equal to half a year's sea pay of an ensign in the navy.}}
#* {{quote-journal|date=November 12, 2011|work=BBC Sport
|title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15693231.stm International friendly: England 1-0 Spain]
|passage=Capello was missing his son's wedding in Milan to '''take charge''' - yet his reshaped England team gave him cause for a double celebration as they overturned the odds in front of a delighted Wembley gallery.}}

